# STOP — CANONICAL MACHINE ENTRY POINT (read this first)

**This is the canonical machine front door for `hyperpolymath/standards`.**
The canonical *human* front door is `README.adoc`. Every other "what is this
repo" doc (EXPLAINME.adoc, TOPOLOGY.adoc, QUICKSTART-*.adoc, llm-warmup-*.md) is a
thin pointer back to one of these two.

## WHAT IS THIS REPO?

The organization-wide standards monorepo: ~30 specs that govern every
Hyperpolymath project — K9 self-validating
components, the protocols, the readiness-grading frameworks (ARG/FRG/CRG/TRG),
RSR compliance, and the enforcement/CI that makes them stick.

## ROUTING — where to go for X (machine index)

| If you want… | Go to |
|---|---|
| K9 foundation (Stream 1) | `1-formats/k9/`, `1-formats/contractiles/` |
| Language policy (Stream 2) | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` |
| Protocols | `*-protocol/` |
| Readiness grades | `adoption-readiness-grades/`, `foundations-readiness-grades/`, `component-readiness-grades/`, `toolchain-readiness-grades/` |
| Multi-repository task scope | `docs/MULTI-REPOSITORY-SCOPE-STANDARD.adoc`; illustrative declaration: `docs/repo-scope.example.toml` |
| Enforcement / CI | `.github/workflows/`, `hooks/` |
| Drift / staleness automation | `hypatia-rules/`; reusable-pin freshness: `docs/decisions/ADR-003-workflow-pin-staleness-window.adoc`, `scripts/check-workflow-staleness.sh`, `scripts/propagate-workflow-pins.sh` |
| Derived architecture map | `TOPOLOGY.adoc` (do not edit) |
| Current project state | `.machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml` |
| Education layer (deep docs, by audience) | `docs/wikis/` (Users / Developers / Maintainers); machine mirror `docs/wikis/0.2-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml` |

## CORE INVARIANTS

1. **No A2ML duplication** — root must NOT contain STATE.a2ml, META.a2ml, etc.
2. **Single source of truth** — `.machine_readable/descriptiles/` is authoritative for state.
3. **Licence is Manual-Only for agents** — every file's licence/SPDX is set by
   the owner. Agents NEVER edit, sweep, or relicense `LICENSE` files or SPDX
   headers; licence drift is FLAG-ONLY (`:review`). See `LICENSE`,
   `.machine_readable/licensing-policy.toml`, and `.claude/CLAUDE.md`.
4. **Author attribution** — "Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>".

## SESSION STARTUP CHECKLIST

- Read THIS file, then `README.adoc`.
- Read `.machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml` for current status + blockers.
- Read `.machine_readable/descriptiles/AGENTIC.a2ml` for interaction patterns.
- Read `.claude/CLAUDE.md` for the language + licence policy (binding).

